{#
  The edge's own probe target, and the only route on this cluster whose whole job is to prove
  that Traefik built a routing table at all.

  If Traefik's boot-time download of the CrowdSec bouncer plugin times out
  (`context deadline exceeded` against plugins.traefik.io), Traefik keeps running without the
  plugin, so `spec.plugin.bouncer` in the `crowdsec` Middleware resolves to "invalid middleware
  type", and the https entrypoint's middleware chain names that Middleware — which rejects
  EVERY router on the entrypoint. The pod stays 3/3 Ready with `/ping` answering 200 while
  every host in the homelab 404s.

  This route is the startupProbe's target (deployment.yaml.j2). It sits on the `https`
  entrypoint on purpose: that entrypoint's chain in static-config.yaml.j2 carries
  `{{ k8s_namespace }}-crowdsec@kubernetescrd`, so this router is rejected by exactly the
  failure the probe exists to catch, and the probe 404s instead of 200ing. Moving it to
  another entrypoint would leave the probe passing while detecting nothing — ENFORCED by
  tests/services/traefik/test_traefik_edge_selfcheck.py against the RENDERED manifests.

  `ping@internal` is Traefik's own ping handler, reached by name with `kind: TraefikService`
  and no port, the same shape and trap as the dashboard's `api@internal`: with the default
  kind Traefik looks for a k8s Service of that name and 404s silently. It is deliberately NOT
  a real backend: pointing the probe at an app would couple the edge's boot to that app being
  up, and a startupProbe failure restarts the edge.

  No Authelia: a 302 scores as probe success, but it makes an Authelia outage crashloop the
  ingress edge.

  Gated on traefik_k8s_manage_crowdsec together with the probe: with the flag false there is
  no plugin, no crowdsec Middleware and no failure mode. The response body is the literal `OK`
  Traefik's ping handler writes, so nothing about the fleet leaks through it.
#}
apiVersion: traefik.io/v1alpha1
kind: IngressRoute
metadata:
  name: traefik-edge-selfcheck
  namespace: {{ k8s_namespace }}
spec:
  entryPoints:
    - https
  routes:
    - kind: Rule
      # Path-only, not Host(): a kubelet probe sends no SNI, so a Host() router answers it 421 and
      # the probe never passes, crashlooping the edge on the change it protects.
      match: "PathPrefix(`/.well-known/traefik-edge-selfcheck`)"
      services:
        # kind + absent port are both load-bearing. See the header.
        - name: ping@internal
          kind: TraefikService
  # No tls block means a non-TLS router, never matched by HTTPS requests.
  tls:
{% if k8s_tls_cert_resolver %}
    certResolver: {{ k8s_tls_cert_resolver }}
{% endif %}
    options:
      name: modern
{% if k8s_tls_cert_resolver %}
    domains:
      - main: "{{ domain }}"
        sans:
          - "*.{{ domain }}"
          - "*.local.{{ domain }}"
{% endif %}
